<h2>5. Crucial Advice for Indian PC Build Buyers</h2>

<p>Over the years of helping students at Editors Gurukul configure rigs across Mumbai, Delhi, Bengaluru, and tier-2 cities, here are practical realities no foreign tech review covers:</p>

<ol>
<li><strong>Never Skip an Online UPS:</strong> Indian electrical grids experience voltage spikes, sags, and random 2-second trips during monsoon or peak summer load. A sudden power trip during a database save in DaVinci Resolve can corrupt your entire Project Library! Invest ₹8,000 in an APC or Microtek 1000VA UPS with AVR (Automatic Voltage Regulation).</li>
<li><strong>Where to Buy Genuine Hardware Online:</strong> Avoid obscure roadside computer dealers selling grey-market imports without brand serial warranties. Trusted Indian online computer component sellers with genuine GST invoicing include:
    <ul>
        <li><strong>MDComputers.in</strong> (Kolkata/All-India delivery)</li>
        <li><strong>PrimeABGB.com</strong> (Lamington Road, Mumbai)</li>
        <li><strong>VedantComputers.com</strong> & <strong>PCStudio.in</strong> (Bengaluru)</li>
        <li><strong>Amazon India</strong> (Only check if the seller is Appario Retail or official brand storefronts)</li>
    </ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Separate Your Drives (The 3-Drive Discipline):</strong> Stop dumping your operating system, games, torrents, and raw video footage onto a single drive! Keep Drive C: strictly for Windows & software. Use Drive D: (Fastest NVMe SSD) strictly for the currently editing project and Resolve media cache. Once the client approves and pays, offload everything to a cheap 5400RPM Seagate/WD external HDD!</li>
</ol>

<h2>FAQ</h2>

<details><summary>Is Intel QuickSync really that important for Adobe Premiere Pro and DaVinci?</summary>
<p>If you edit footage from consumer mirrorless cameras (Sony A7 IV, Canon R6, GoPro, DJI Drones) that shoot H.264 or H.265 4:2:2 10-bit codec, yes! Intel's integrated GPU inside non-F series chips (like i5-14600K or i7-14700K) features QuickSync hardware decoders that play back these heavy files instantly without making proxies! AMD chips require brute CPU cores or NVIDIA decoding (which doesn't always support 4:2:2 10-bit decryptions natively). Always get non-F Intel chips if editing mirrorless footage!</p>
</details>

<details><summary>Can I build a video editing rig without a dedicated graphics card?</summary>
<p>Only if you are sticking to barebone 1080p cuts without color grading or effects. The moment you drop a blur effect, noise reduction, or try to balance colors in DaVinci Resolve on integrated graphics, your timeline will drop to 3 FPS and become completely unplayable. Dedicated VRAM is non-negotiable for real creators.</p>
</details>

<details><summary>Why shouldn't I buy a single 32GB RAM stick and upgrade later?</summary>
<p>Because video editors rely massively on Memory Bandwidth to shovel gigabytes of frame data to the GPU per second. Running a single stick forces your processor into single-channel mode, literally cutting memory transfer throughput by half! Always install RAM in matched pairs (16GB x 2 sticks for 32GB total) in slots A2 and B2 of your motherboard to activate high-speed Dual-Channel mode!</p>
</details>

<details><summary>Should I install NVIDIA Game Ready Drivers or Studio Drivers?</summary>
<p>Always go to GeForce Experience or NVIDIA app and toggle to install <strong>NVIDIA Studio Drivers</strong>. Game Ready drivers receive constant weekly beta patches for new game launches that can inadvertently break video decoding pipelines or cause random Direct3D/CUDA runtime crashes inside DaVinci Resolve and Premiere during rendering. Studio drivers are certified specifically against stable production software releases.</p>
</details>

